Chocolate Shipments Sales Analysis – Power BI Dashboard

An interactive Power BI report that analyses chocolate shipment data (2023 onwards) to track sales, costs, profit, shipment volumes, and sales-team performance across products and geographies.

📌** Project Overview**

A chocolate manufacturer ships products to multiple countries through a team of sales people. This project turns the raw shipment records into a dashboard that answers questions such as:

Which products and countries generate the most revenue and profit?
How do shipments, boxes sold and amount trend month by month?
Which sales people perform best (amount, boxes, profit %)?
What is the typical shipment size (boxes per shipment)?


Sheet	Description	Key columns
Shipments (~25,000 rows)	Fact table, one row per shipment	ShipmentID, SPID, PID, GID, Shipdate, Amount, Boxes, Order_Status
Dimension Data	Lookup tables for products, locations and people	Product, Category, Cost_per_box, PID · Geo, Region, GID · Sales_person, Team, Picture, SPID
Calendar	Date table	cal_date, Month_num, month_name, year, weekday_num, weekday_name
Measure	Meaning
Total Amount	= Sum of shipment revenue
Total Boxes =	Sum of boxes shipped
Shipment Count =	Number of shipments
Total Costs=	Boxes × cost per box
Total Profit =	Total Amount − Total Costs
Profit % =	Total Profit ÷ Total Amount
Amount per Box	= Total Amount ÷ Total Boxes
